.go by commit count, with no line share. It mentions Mei Chen's commit but doesn't credit her with the Time7 accessor at about 9% of lines.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer A follows the history to database_sql.go and names the original authors as gone. It gives no share for Justin Overfelt. It lists Wheeler first and doesn't name Overfelt as the largest author with 44%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer A names Sam Okafor and Noor Haddad as active and recommends Ravi Menon for everything. It gives no 93-98% figure for lines owned by departed people. It doesn't treat Alex Rowe as the only other active person alongside Kofi Mensah.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer A lists Noor Haddad and Sam Okafor as active contributors and suggests Sam Okafor as a second reviewer for time.go. That treats them as experts, which the criterion forbids.\",\"pass\":false}],\n\"B\": [{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer B names Paul Borman as the main author of time.go with 73.0% of lines (70.9% excluding blank lines). It marks him inactive and excludes the line-ending commit. It also says his last commit was 2016, which is wrong (truth 2023), and it leaves his identities unmerged. The substance matches the criterion on author, share and no longer active.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer B names MikeWang as main author of version7.go at 81.2%. It credits Mei Chen with the Time7 accessor at about 9.4% and says Ravi committed it but owns only 2 lines.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer B follows the history of database_sql.go from sql.go. It names Justin Overfelt at 44.1% as the largest author, with Stone and Wheeler. It says all of them are inactive.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer B says no active person holds a meaningful share of time.go or the SQL code. It gives no repo-wide 95.9% figure for departed owners. It notes Alex Rowe as the single active person but doesn't merge the identities. It lists Ravi and Mei as active. It also calls Alexander Rowe 'inactive' in the time.go table, which is inconsistent with the later note, and it never mentions Kofi Mensah.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer B doesn't credit Noor Haddad or Sam Okafor with any ownership. It ignores the line-ending commit. It doesn't discuss the bot commits or Kofi Mensah's 1970 author date. The core of the criterion is met, but the bot and Kofi parts aren't addressed.\",\"pass\":true}],\n\"C\": [{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer C names Paul Borman as the time.go main author by commit count (6 commits) with no line share. It dates his last commit to 2021, which is wrong. It says he is effectively gone, but it doesn't give the 65-80% share.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer C credits Mei Chen with the Time7 accessor and lists Ravi Menon as the latest committer. It gives no line shares and doesn't name MikeWang as the main author with about 81%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer C follows the history of sql.go to database_sql.go. It lists the authors by commit count, with Wheeler first, and gives no Overfelt share. It doesn't name Overfelt as the largest author.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer C gives no figure for lines owned by departed people. It lists Ravi, Rowe, Mei and Kofi as recent, and it treats Alex Rowe as one person. It still doesn't state the 95.9% figure or the line shares per file.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer C names Sam Okafor as a time.go author and flags Kofi's 1970 date as a bad timestamp. It says Kofi's activity can't be determined, so it doesn't treat him as active. It doesn't treat Sam Okafor as an owner, but it lists him among the main authors of time.go.\",\"pass\":false}],\n\"D\": [{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer D credits Sam Okafor with 100% of time.go by blame. It later says the credit is misleading, but it never names Paul Borman as the 73% author. The criterion lists crediting Sam Okafor as a failure.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer D names MikeWang as the main author of version7.go (101 of 117 lines, 86%) and credits Mei Chen with Time7. It gives no Mei share. It says Ravi's and Mei's changes were small. The MikeWang share of 86% is within the 72-90% range, but the Mei share is missing.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer D follows the history of sql.go to database_sql.go. It names Justin Overfelt as the largest author at 26 of 59 lines (44%), with Stone, Wheeler and Souza. It says all of them are inactive.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives no 95.9% figure for departed owners. It doesn't treat Alex Rowe as one merged identity. It says nobody committed in the last 90 days, which is not the 12-month window the criterion asks about.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer D credits Sam Okafor with 100% of time.go in its main table, although it caveats that this is misleading. It treats Kofi's 1970 date as a bad timestamp. Sam Okafor owning 100% in the main table fails the criterion.\",\"pass\":false}],\n\"E\": [{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer E calls Sam Okafor's 100% blame credit misleading and names Paul Borman as the real original author. It gives no line share for Borman and says his last commit was 2021, which is wrong (truth 2023). The criterion requires the 65-80% share.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer E names MikeWang at 86% of version7.go, within the 72-90% range. It credits Mei Chen with Time7 at 9%. It doesn't credit Ravi Menon with those lines.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer E follows the history of database_sql.go from sql.go. It names Justin Overfelt at 44% as the largest author, with Stone, Souza and Wheeler. It says all of them are inactive and that Ravi only did the rename.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer E doesn't give the 93-98% share of lines owned by departed people. It doesn't say clearly that Alex Rowe is one person with about 3%, and it asks whether the two 'Rowe' identities are the same. It doesn't list Kofi Mensah as active. It names Ravi Menon as the only active person.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer E says Sam Okafor's blame credit is misleading and doesn't name him an owner. It doesn't credit Noor Haddad. It flags Kofi's 1970 date as a bad timestamp, not as being inactive since 1970. It doesn't discuss the bot commits.\",\"pass\":true}],\n\"F\": [{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer F says Paul Borman wrote almost all of time.go. It gives no line share and says nothing about 73%. It also says he has no commits in the last 12 months, but it doesn't give his last-commit year.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer F lists MikeWang and Mei Chen for version7.go with no line shares. It doesn't credit Mei with the Time7 accessor, and it gives no Ravi-versus-Mei committer/author split.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer F admits it didn't run the per-file history on database_sql.go. It lists Wheeler first and gives no Overfelt share. It doesn't name Overfelt as the largest author.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer F names the active people as Ravi Menon, Alexander Rowe and Kofi Mensah, which matches the ground truth, and counts Rowe as one person. It gives no 93-98% share of departed lines. It also cites a 12-month window and lists a bot among the committers.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer F treats Kofi Mensah as active and calls renovate[bot] a bot, not a person. It names Sam Okafor as a time.go contributor with a 2025 commit. It doesn't call him an owner. It doesn't discuss Noor Haddad. The criterion is met for the bot and Kofi.\",\"pass\":true}]}","ttft_ms":19600,"type":"result","duration_ms":19621,"uuid":"e362bdda-80db-452c-8bde-6ff64fb27f20","ttft_stream_ms":1892,"time_to_request_ms":448,"first_content_frame_ms":1892,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
